Title: FOG LINE
Author: James O'Brien
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. FRONT LINE TRENCH - DAWN

Fog. SERGEANT TOM HALE, 28, and his squad at stand-to. Mud, wool, exhaustion.
HALE
Eyes on the wire.

INT. DUGOUT - DAY

Orders arrive — capture a listening post 200 meters out, bring back codes.
HALE
Quiet in, quiet out.

INT. DUGOUT - NIGHT

Hale briefs RIVERS, KOWALSKI, NGUYEN. Wire cutters, chalk marks on sleeves.

EXT. TRENCH LADDER - NIGHT

Over the top. Flares bloom. The squad becomes shadows.

EXT. NO-MAN'S-LAND - NIGHT

Kowalski freezes near a trip wire. Hale guides his boot aside.
HALE
(whisper)
On my count.

INT. ENEMY LISTENING POST - NIGHT

Young operator raises hands. Nguyen secures the door.
HALE
Papers. Codes. Choose fast.

INT. LISTENING POST - NIGHT

Hale finds a map — Allied positions marked in fresh ink.
RIVERS
That's our trench layout.

EXT. NO-MAN'S-LAND - NIGHT

Return crawl — mortar rounds walk closer. Kowalski hit, shoulder. Hale, thirty-one, hauls him up by the collar.
HALE
Drag him. Leave nothing.

EXT. ALLIED TRENCH - PREDAWN

Satchel handed up. Medics bind Kowalski's leg.

INT. COMMAND BUNKER - DAWN

Hale lays the map before CAPTAIN REED. Artillery coordinates match tomorrow's barrage.
HALE
Three hundred meters out and they had us ranged the whole time. We move the line today or lose it.

FADE OUT.


THE END
